  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Autenticacion",
      "description": "Registro, login y logout con Laravel Sanctum. Los *Login* guardan el token en `{{token}}`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Registro",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text",
                "description": "Imprescindible en Laravel: sin esta cabecera, los errores de validacion o autenticacion devuelven HTML o redirigen en vez de JSON."
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Crea un usuario nuevo con rol `customer`.\n\n**Auth:** no requiere token.\n\n**Campos obligatorios:** `name`, `first_surname`, `second_surname`, `email`, `password`.\nEl resto (`address`, `phone_number`, `birthdate`, `dni`, `postal_code`, `city`) son opcionales.\n\n**Respuestas:** `201` creado, `422` error de validacion (por ejemplo, email ya registrado).\n\n> Cambia el email en cada ejecucion: `email` es unico en la base de datos.\n\n> `email_verified_at` no se envia: queda en `NULL` (verificacion de email pendiente).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Nuevo\",\n  \"first_surname\": \"Usuario\",\n  \"second_surname\": \"Prueba\",\n  \"email\": \"nuevo.{{$timestamp}}@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Customer1234!\",\n  \"password_confirmation\": \"Customer1234!\",\n  \"phone_number\": \"600999888\",\n  \"birthdate\": \"1999-01-15\",\n  \"dni\": \"{{dni}}\",\n  \"postal_code\": \"29001\",\n  \"city\": \"Malaga\",\n  \"role\": \"customer\",\n  \"is_active\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status 201 o 200\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// DNI distinto en cada ejecucion (la columna dni es unica)",
                  "pm.variables.set('dni', String(Math.floor(10000000 + Math.random() * 89999999)) + 'H');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "201 Creado",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "url": {
                  "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
                  "host": [
                    "{{baseUrl}}"
                  ],
                  "path": [
                    "auth",
                    "register"
                  ]
                }
              },
              "status": "Created",
              "code": 201,
              "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
              "header": [
                {
                  "key": "Content-Type",
                  "value": "application/json"
                }
              ],
              "body": "{\n  \"message\": \"Usuario registrado\",\n  \"user\": {\n    \"id\": 8,\n    \"name\": \"Nuevo\",\n    \"email\": \"nuevo@example.com\",\n    \"role\": \"customer\"\n  }\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (cliente)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text",
                "description": "Imprescindible en Laravel: sin esta cabecera, los errores de validacion o autenticacion devuelven HTML o redirigen en vez de JSON."
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Inicia sesion como **cliente** y guarda el token en `{{token}}` (sobrescribe el del admin).\n\nCredenciales: `carlos@example.com` / `Customer1234!`\n\nUtil para comprobar que un cliente **no** puede acceder a rutas de administrador (debe devolver `403`).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"carlos@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Customer1234!\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Guarda el token del cliente en {{tokenCliente}} (no pisa el token del admin).",
                  "// Se usa solo en la peticion que comprueba que un cliente no puede listar usuarios.",
                  "pm.test(\"Status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const token = json.token || (json.data && json.data.token) || json.access_token;",
                  "pm.test(\"La respuesta contiene un token\", () => pm.expect(token).to.be.a(\"string\").and.not.empty);",
                  "if (token) { pm.collectionVariables.set(\"tokenCliente\", token); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (usuario inactivo)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text",
                "description": "Imprescindible en Laravel: sin esta cabecera, los errores de validacion o autenticacion devuelven HTML o redirigen en vez de JSON."
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Prueba negativa: `marta@example.com` tiene `is_active = 0`.\n\n**Esperado:** que la API rechace el login (`401`, `403` o `422`, segun tu implementacion). Si devuelve `200` y un token, falta comprobar `is_active` en el controlador de login.\n\nCredenciales: `marta@example.com` / `Customer1234!`",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"marta@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Customer1234!\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Se rechaza el login\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([401, 403, 422]));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (contrasena incorrecta)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text",
                "description": "Imprescindible en Laravel: sin esta cabecera, los errores de validacion o autenticacion devuelven HTML o redirigen en vez de JSON."
